PediQUEST reports were valued by children, parents, and providers and contributed at least sometimes to physician       
initiation of a psychosocial consult (56%). CONCLUSION Although routine feedback of PROs did not significantly affect   
the child\\'s symptoms or HRQoL, changes were in expected directions and improvements observed in emotional HRQoL       
through exploratory analyses were encouraging. Importantly, children, parents, and providers value PRO feedback."},     
{"study_index": 60, "title": "Rates of detection of developmental problems at the 18-month well-baby visit by family    
